Just like the below, define script to set HTML content OK and Offline

Html content is

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<body>
    <p>Status: OK</p>
</body>
</html>

$IndexFilePath = "C:\inetpub\wwwroot\Healthcheck.html"
$LogFile = "C:\log\Set_Component_Status.log"

This script should also include iisreset command

Create one script for OK and the other for OFFLINE







# Define path to index.html and log file
$IndexFilePath = "C:\inetpub\wwwroot\index.html"
$LogFile = "E:\Installation Media\Script\Set_Component_Status.log"

# Define Online HTML content
$OnlineHTML = @"
<html>
<body>
<p>Online</p>
</body>
</html>
"@

# Write the Online content
$OnlineHTML | Set-Content -Path $IndexFilePath -Force

# Log the change
$Timestamp = Get-Date -Format "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss"
"[$Timestamp] Status set to ONLINE" | Add-Content -Path $LogFile

Write-Host "✔ CCP node status set to ONLINE and logged."
